<!--
  World fragment loaded via Include src= (see index.html shell).
  Edit this file — do not paste into index.html.

  South-east rock field. gen_terrain.py already raises and roughens this corner
  (a broad shoulder plus 45 m-wavelength noise), so the props sit on ground that
  reads as broken rather than on a lawn with boulders dropped on it.

  max-slope-deg is deliberately high here (60-68): rocks are the one thing that
  should cling to the steep shoulders. Note the slope test re-draws a new random
  position up to max-slope-attempts times and then simply omits the instance, so
  actual counts on steep ground land below `count`.
-->
